 "summary": "Wirth's radically simplified successor to Modula-2, designed together with the Oberon operating system: modules, record type extension (single inheritance) with type tests and guards, garbage collection, and a report of about 16 pages. Oberon-2 (1991) added type-bound procedures; Oberon-07 (2007/2016) is Wirth's final, further reduced revision.",
 "status": "maintained",
